# .git stays IN the context so the builder can stamp `semsource version` with
# `git describe` when no VERSION arg is passed (compose-packaging-hardening D5:
# a compose-built image must identify itself, not report "dev").
.github
.claude
docs
test
coverage.out
*.md
LICENSE
configs

# The root image is a Go-only build (`go build ./cmd/semsource`); the workbench
# ships as its own image built from the ./ui context with its own .dockerignore
# (docker-compose.ui-dev.yml). Nothing under ui/ is compiled or embedded here,
# so shipping it — 159MB of node_modules alone — only slows every context
# upload and busts the `COPY . .` layer on unrelated frontend churn. If Go ever
# go:embeds built UI assets, narrow this to `ui/node_modules` rather than
# dropping the rule.
ui
